  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Desk Study - DETAILED DESIGN OF MAGDALENA RIVER PORT, through Ascendant Program Services, LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $7,500 Desk Study reviews a proposal for the detailed design and preparation of construction documents for the Magdalena River port project being developed by Terminal Fluvial Andalucia, S.A., an affiliate of Sociedad Portuaria Regional de Cartagena, S.A. (SPRC), the concessionaire of the ports of Cartagena and Contecar on Colombia&apos;s Caribbean coast. The river terminal is intended to handle 60,000 TEUs per year, comprised of a variety of commodities that are considered to benefit from reduced transportation costs between the marine terminals in Cartagena and Barranquilla and inland destinations within Colombia. The design effort will focus on terminal property of 365 hectares (more than 900 acres), which is located three kilometers away from one of the country&apos;s main roads and railroads.</narrative>
  </description>
